# Triage Issue Skill Activation Rule

When user intent indicates bug investigation that should end with a tracked GitHub issue, use the `triage-issue` skill from `.cursor/skills/triage-issue/SKILL.md` before implementation.

## Trigger signals

Apply this rule when the user:

- asks to triage a bug or investigate root cause
- asks to create/file a GitHub issue from findings
- asks for a TDD-based fix plan for a reported bug
- asks to connect triage output to GitHub Project tracking

## Expected behavior

- Investigate first, then identify root cause.
- Produce a concrete RED-GREEN TDD fix plan.
- Create issue via `gh issue create` without unnecessary review pauses.
- Add the created issue to GitHub Project `https://github.com/users/vojtechbarta/projects/1`.
- Set project `Status` to `To triage`.
- Treat project add/status failures as workflow failures and output remediation commands.

## Non-goals

- Do not use this skill for feature brainstorming without a concrete bug report.
- Do not skip project tracking for issue triage workflows.
